1
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:05,120
The reason I asked you to brunch...

2
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:08,540
...is because I've been thinking about my maid of honor.

3
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:10,750
Oh, my God. This is it. Oh.

4
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:12,840
I hope it's you.

5
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:14,880
- I hope it's you.     - Me too.

6
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:18,850
First of all, I love you both so much.

7
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:23,060
- You're both so important to me.     - Blah, blah, blah. Who is it?

8
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:26,730
I was thinking we could come up with a system...

9
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:29,110
...where we trade off being maid of honor.

10
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:32,610
- Hypothetically, if Phoebe were mine...     - Yes! Oh.

11
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,740
Hypothetically.

12
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,070
Still.

13
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:42,410
If Phoebe were mine, Rachel would be Phoebe's, I'd be Rachel's.

14
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:45,250
We all get to do it and no one gets upset.

15
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:49,750
- That's a pretty good idea.     - I'll do that. So who's yours?

16
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:54,670
Well, that's the best part. You guys get to decide.

17
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:59,850
- Why is that the best part?     - I don't have to.

18
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:06,350
Of course we'll help you decide. We'll do anything we can to help you.

19
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:08,020
I'd like to make a toast.

20
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,320
To the future Mrs. Chandler Bing...

21
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:15,530
...my best friend and truly one of the nicest people that...

22
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,360
- Really not deciding.     - Fine.

23
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:22,910
Excuse me, I couldn't help overhearing.

24
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:25,580
- You're marrying Chandler Bing?     - Yeah.

25
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:26,870
Huh.

26
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,170
Good luck!

27
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:32,290
Oh, and good luck to you too!

28
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:34,670
What a nice lady.

29
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:17,510
Yeah!

30
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:21,090
- Die Hard, still great.     - Yep.

31
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:23,140
Let's make it a double feature?

32
00:02:23,350 --> 00:02:24,600
What else did you rent?

33
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:27,180
Die Hard 2.

34
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:30,100
Joey, this is Die Hard 1 again.

35
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:35,570
Well, we'll watch it a second time and it's Die Hard 2.

36
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:39,400
- Joey, we just saw it.     - And?

37
00:02:39,610 --> 00:02:41,700
It would be cool to see it again!

38
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:44,700
- Yeah! Die Hard!     - Die Hard!

39
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:48,370
Dude, you didn't say Die Hard.

40
00:02:49,290 --> 00:02:50,870
Is everything okay?

41
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:53,830
Yeah, I just got plans.

42
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,340
Well, John McClane had plans.

43
00:02:58,050 --> 00:03:01,300
I want to leave before Joey gets all worked up...

44
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:03,890
...and starts calling everybody "bitch."

45
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:08,020
What are you talking about, bitch?

46
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:12,600
- Hey, Rachel.     - Yeah?

47
00:03:12,810 --> 00:03:16,400
When I get married, will you be my maid of honor?

48
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:17,980
Really?

49
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:21,530
Oh, my God, Phoebe. I mean, I'm just...

50
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:23,200
Wait a minute.

51
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:30,160
If I'm your maid of honor, that means that you are Monica's.

52
00:03:30,330 --> 00:03:32,120
Oh.

53
00:03:33,290 --> 00:03:35,540
- Well, if that's what you want.     - Oh!

54
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:39,170
No way, Phoebe. I want to be Monica's.

55
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:42,670
- Why does it even matter?     - Why does it matter to you?

56
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:45,300
Because this one is now.

57
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:48,060
And it's two of our best friends.

58
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:50,180
And who knows what you're gonna marry.

59
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:56,190
What if I marry Ross? Or Joey?

60
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:59,360
You wouldn't.

61
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:04,910
Okay, look, Rachel. I know you really want to do this...

62
00:04:05,110 --> 00:04:08,450
...but I've never been maid of honor to anyone before.

63
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,870
I know you've done it at least twice.

64
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:14,080
- Yeah, but, Phoebe...     - Please let me finish.

65
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:17,210
I guess that was it.

66
00:04:19,090 --> 00:04:20,590
Okay.

67
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:24,840
Okay. Since you've never done it before, you can be Monica's maid of honor.

68
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:27,050
Oh, thank you so much!

69
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,350
Yay.

70
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,060
I'm gonna marry someone good.

71
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:36,730
Oh, I know.

72
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:39,310
- Better than Chandler.     - Pfft.

73
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,460
- What happened?     - I don't know.

74
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:04,590
We fell asleep. That is all.

75
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,630
Yeah. Yeah? Yeah.

76
00:05:08,970 --> 00:05:10,970
All right, well, I'd better go.

77
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:13,100
- I think that would be best.     - Yeah.

78
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:15,020
- I'll talk to you later.     - Okay.

79
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:18,650
- But not about this.     - No, never. Never!

80
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,270
- So, uh...   - Uh...

81
00:05:22,150 --> 00:05:24,360
- Bye.     - No touch. No touch.

82
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:30,450
Hey, a weird thing happened at brunch.

83
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:32,950
This woman overheard that I was marrying you...

84
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:35,330
...and she wished me good luck.

85
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:36,790
That's sweet.

86
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:39,960
No, it was more like a "good luck."

87
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:43,630
So, what did this woman look like?

88
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:46,130
She was like 30, dark hair, attractive.

89
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:50,890
Any chance you were looking into a bright, shiny thing called a mirror?

90
00:05:51,390 --> 00:05:53,600
Was it someone you dated in college?

91
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:56,100
No, I only dated two girls in college...

92
00:05:56,270 --> 00:05:59,770
...both blond, both not attractive.

93
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:02,270
Let me check this out.

94
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:05,110
- What are you doing?     - Well, let's see.

95
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:08,200
Okay, uh, is that her?

96
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,820
Oh, my God, yes!

97
00:06:09,990 --> 00:06:14,030
- Who is she?     - Julie Graff, my camp girlfriend.

98
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:15,830
Did you break up with her?

99
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:19,330
No, we're still together.

100
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:26,840
We went out for two summers and then I broke up with her.

101
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:29,010
- Why?     - She came back the third summer...

102
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:32,720
...and she'd gotten really fa... Ahh.

103
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:38,560
- Fat?      - I did not say fat.

104
00:06:38,730 --> 00:06:41,100
I said fa... Ahh.

105
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:45,480
You broke up with a girl because she was fat?

106
00:06:45,650 --> 00:06:47,440
Yeah. Yeah.

107
00:06:47,610 --> 00:06:51,990
But it was a really long time ago. Does she still feel bad?

108
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:53,530
Apparently she does.

109
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:56,990
You know what they say, "Elephants never forget."

110
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:03,330
Seriously, good luck marrying me.

111
00:07:07,590 --> 00:07:08,920
Hey, what's going on?

112
00:07:09,090 --> 00:07:11,090
Phoebe is gonna be Monica's maid of honor.

113
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:15,850
Hey. Hope it goes better than the last time you did it for that girl downstairs.

114
00:07:17,890 --> 00:07:20,560
You have been maid of honor before?

115
00:07:20,730 --> 00:07:24,650
You see? This is exactly why you shouldn't lie.

116
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:27,440
That's it. I am maid of honor.

117
00:07:27,610 --> 00:07:29,780
- No, I am.     - How come you are?

118
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:32,570
Because I cared enough to lie.

119
00:07:32,990 --> 00:07:35,700
Hey, I could help you decide who should do it.

120
00:07:35,870 --> 00:07:37,620
We could have an audition.

121
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:40,700
See how you'd handle maid-of-honor-type situations.

122
00:07:40,870 --> 00:07:43,080
- What are you talking about?     - When I want a job...

123
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:46,290
...I audition and if I'm the best of the people they see...

124
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,090
...they give me the part.

125
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:50,710
Okay, so after this audition, who decides who gets it?

126
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:53,130
Oh, me and Ross can be the judges.

127
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:56,220
- It's better than us deciding.     - Oh, this is crazy.

128
00:07:56,390 --> 00:08:00,390
- Can't we just flip a coin?     - No, coins hate me.

129
00:08:00,890 --> 00:08:05,190
Okay, fine. You know what? We will let Ross and Joey decide.

130
00:08:05,730 --> 00:08:07,110
Hi!

131
00:08:07,270 --> 00:08:09,520
Ross, sweetie.

132
00:08:11,740 --> 00:08:14,650
Hey there, handsome thing.

133
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:22,910
Wow, this cologne really is every bit as good as Giorgio.

134
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,130
Hey.

135
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:33,420
Just brought back your videos.

136
00:08:33,590 --> 00:08:37,550
Hey, Ross. Look, I think we need to talk about before.

137
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,970
No. No, we don't.

138
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:41,140
Yes, we do.

139
00:08:41,770 --> 00:08:44,940
Now, look. That was the best nap I ever had.

140
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:52,530
I don't know what you're talking about.

141
00:08:53,070 --> 00:08:54,740
Come on, admit it.

142
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,950
That was the best nap you ever had.

143
00:08:58,030 --> 00:08:59,870
I've had better.

144
00:09:01,410 --> 00:09:03,620
Okay. When?

145
00:09:04,910 --> 00:09:07,960
All right! All right! It was the best nap ever!

146
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:09,670
- Ah!     - I said it, okay?

147
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,920
But it's over, Joey!

148
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,380
I want to do it again.

149
00:09:19,470 --> 00:09:21,470
We can't do it again.

150
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:24,350
- Why not?     - Because it's weird!

151
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:27,310
Fine.

152
00:09:28,350 --> 00:09:29,440
You want a drink?

153
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:33,190
- Sure. What do you got?      - Warm milk and Excedrin PM.

154
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:42,030
Chandler.

155
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:44,910
I just figured out who you are.

156
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,580
Can you figure out what I'm doing?

157
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:51,420
- You're Louis Posen.     - Who?

158
00:09:52,250 --> 00:09:55,050
He was my best friend in fifth grade.

159
00:09:55,210 --> 00:09:58,470
One day, I asked him to be my boyfriend and he said no.

160
00:09:58,630 --> 00:09:59,970
Do you know why?

161
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:04,350
Because you kept talking to him while he was trying to go to the bathroom?

162
00:10:04,850 --> 00:10:08,100
No, but because he thought I was too fa... Ahh.

163
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:13,400
Every time I think about it, I feel as bad as I did then.

164
00:10:13,570 --> 00:10:16,360
I really think you should apologize to Julie.

165
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:19,610
Honey, are you kidding? That was like 16 years ago.

166
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:22,990
It would make me feel better if Louis apologized to me.

167
00:10:23,830 --> 00:10:27,250
I'll do it. But I warn you, this may make me a better person.

168
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:30,460
And that is not the man you fell in love with.

169
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,880
This is how it's gonna work.

170
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:36,630
We'll give you hypothetical maid-of-honor situations.

171
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:39,090
You'll be scored on a scale of one to 10.

172
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:41,720
- One being the highest.     - Ten is the highest.

173
00:10:41,890 --> 00:10:44,510
- Why is 10 the highest?     - Because it's the highest.

174
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:50,350
Okay, Rachel, you're up first.

175
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:53,400
Situation number one: You're with Monica.

176
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:57,690
The wedding is about to start when Monica gets cold feet. Go!

177
00:10:57,940 --> 00:11:00,280
I don't want to marry Chandler.

178
00:11:00,450 --> 00:11:02,610
- I've got cold feet.     - It's gonna be okay.

179
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:05,410
One man the rest of my life? I don't know.

180
00:11:05,580 --> 00:11:08,080
This means I'll never get to sleep with Joey.

181
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:12,670
Look, Monica...

182
00:11:12,830 --> 00:11:14,710
...getting cold feet is very common.

183
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:17,550
It's just because of all the anticipation.

184
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:21,930
And you just have to remember that you love Chandler.

185
00:11:22,090 --> 00:11:24,680
And also, I ran out on a wedding.

186
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:27,640
You don't get to keep the gifts.

187
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:30,390
Very good, drawing on your own experience.

188
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,940
Very good.

189
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:34,480
Yes, very nice, Rachel.

190
00:11:34,650 --> 00:11:35,940
Thank you, judges.

191
00:11:36,110 --> 00:11:38,110
- Kiss-ass.     - Oh.

192
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:42,610
- Okay, Phoebe.     - Yes, Your Honor.

193
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:45,160
We're now in the ceremony.

194
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:47,410
Monica is about to say, "I do"...

195
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:49,990
...when her drunk uncle starts yelling.

196
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:51,580
What do you do? Go!

197
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:54,420
When Monica was a little girl...

198
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:55,670
...I remember that...

199
00:11:59,340 --> 00:12:00,760
Ow!

200
00:12:01,010 --> 00:12:02,510
- Very good!     - Oh.

201
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,220
Yes, excellent. Perfect score.

202
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:08,760
She just made a scene in the middle of the ceremony!

203
00:12:08,930 --> 00:12:11,770
Hey, you want a little taste of Pheebs?

204
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:17,150
It is time for you to give your maid-of-honor speech.

205
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,900
We haven't even prepared...

206
00:12:19,070 --> 00:12:22,320
- Go!     - Okay, okay, okay. Um...

207
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:25,110
Webster's Dictionary defines marriage as...

208
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:29,660
Okay, no! Forget that! That sucks! Okay, never mind. Forget it. Um, um...

209
00:12:29,910 --> 00:12:34,960
I met... I met Monica when we were just a couple of 6-year-olds...

210
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:40,170
...and became friends with Chandler when he was 25...

211
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:43,130
...although he seemed like a 6-year-old.

212
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:44,970
Oh.

213
00:12:45,550 --> 00:12:48,470
Thank you. Thank you very much. Um...

214
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:52,220
I've known them separately and together.

215
00:12:52,390 --> 00:12:58,020
To know them as a couple is to know that you are truly in the presence of love.

216
00:12:58,190 --> 00:13:01,480
So I would like to raise my glass...

217
00:13:01,650 --> 00:13:03,280
...to Monica and Chandler...

218
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:08,070
...and the beautiful adventure they are about to embark upon together.

219
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:11,950
I can think of no two people better prepared for the journey.

220
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:14,250
Wow.

221
00:13:15,710 --> 00:13:17,960
- Great speech.     - Yeah, it really was.

222
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,250
Oh, thanks.

223
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:24,300
Okay, Phoebe, I guess you're next. Although I really don't see the point.

224
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:28,890
Okay.

225
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:34,560
I can't believe that Monica and Chandler are getting married.

226
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:37,270
I remember talking about this day with Rachel...

227
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:40,610
...while we were showering together, naked.

228
00:13:47,950 --> 00:13:50,030
And she's back in the game!

229
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:00,920
Julie. Hi.

230
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:03,380
Chandler Bing. I guess you remember me.

231
00:14:03,550 --> 00:14:06,010
Hello, Skidmark.

232
00:14:08,470 --> 00:14:11,140
It's a nickname. I'll explain later.

233
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:13,350
It's pretty clear.

234
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:19,310
I owe you a long-overdue apology.

235
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:22,980
I shouldn't have broken up with you because you were overweight.

236
00:14:23,690 --> 00:14:25,730
That's why you broke up with me?

237
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:31,160
You didn't know that?

238
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,450
Well, I guess my work here is done.

239
00:14:38,660 --> 00:14:39,700

240
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:44,590
First of all, I would like to say you both performed very well, okay?

241
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:46,840
You should be proud.

242
00:14:47,010 --> 00:14:51,760
And I'd also like to say, in this competition, there are no losers.

243
00:14:51,930 --> 00:14:54,470
Well, except Rachel. Damn it!

244
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:57,600
Really? I won?

245
00:14:57,770 --> 00:15:00,770
- What?     - I'm sorry, Rach, it was really close.

246
00:15:00,940 --> 00:15:04,690
- Well, then I demand a recount!     - Actually, it wasn't that close.

247
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:07,940
You know what? Your thing was so stupid anyway.

248
00:15:08,110 --> 00:15:10,450
We're gonna flip a coin, all right?

249
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:13,410
Heads. Oh!

250
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:16,830
What? The coins have finally forgiven me!

251
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:21,960
You know what? I hope Monica forgives you after you throw her...

252
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:26,960
...her vegetarian-voodoo-goddess-circle-y shower.

253
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:32,050
Rach, it's gonna be okay. You guys are the best!

254
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:38,010
Boy, I tell you. That judging stuff took a lot out of me.

255
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:39,390
- Yeah?     - Yeah.

256
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:44,060
Thinking about maybe going upstairs and taking a little nap on my couch.

257
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:49,530
Why would I care about that?

258
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:53,740
No reason. I'm just saying that...

259
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:56,240
...that's where I'll be.

260
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:20,010
As bad as that went, I actually enjoyed myself.

261
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:24,520
I think that I'm going to apologize for all the stupid things that I do.

262
00:16:24,690 --> 00:16:27,310
Why don't you just stop doing stupid things?

263
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:31,650
- Then you wouldn't have to apologize.     - I'd love it if I could do both.

264
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:37,660
All right, I have to ask.

265
00:16:37,950 --> 00:16:39,490
What?

266
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:42,700
Will you break up with me if I get fat again?

267
00:16:42,870 --> 00:16:44,080
What?

268
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:47,580
You broke up with Julie. How much weight did she gain?

269
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:50,130
A hundred and forty-five pounds.

270
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:52,800
In one year?

271
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:55,300
My God, what did she eat? Her family?

272
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,430
That's not the point.

273
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:03,600
I know it was a stupid reason to break up with someone, but I was 15.

274
00:17:03,770 --> 00:17:08,060
Yeah, well, that's not the only time this was an issue.

275
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:12,530
You remember when you spent Thanksgiving with us?

276
00:17:12,690 --> 00:17:13,860
You called me fat.

277
00:17:14,030 --> 00:17:15,190
Wait a minute.

278
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:18,110
- That was totally different.     - How?

279
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:22,080
You were not supposed to hear that. I said that behind your back.

280
00:17:23,450 --> 00:17:26,960
What if I have babies, okay? I'm gonna look different.

281
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:29,630
I'm okay with that, but I'm not sure you are.

282
00:17:29,790 --> 00:17:33,090
You have to realize I don't think of you as a thin, beautiful woman.

283
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:41,350
This is one of the things that I can apologize for later.

284
00:17:42,970 --> 00:17:45,430
What I mean is, you're Monica.

285
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:48,730
Okay? And I am in love with Monica.

286
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,480
Keep going.

287
00:17:50,650 --> 00:17:54,860
So you can balloon up or you can shrink down...

288
00:17:55,030 --> 00:17:57,030
...and I will still love you.

289
00:17:58,490 --> 00:18:02,120
Even if I shrink down to 2 inches tall?

290
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:04,910
I'd carry you around in my pocket.

291
00:18:06,290 --> 00:18:07,460
I love you.

292
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:13,750
Skidmark still got a way with the ladies.

293
00:18:16,670 --> 00:18:17,720
Hi, Pheebs.

294
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,340
- Hi.     - Hi.

295
00:18:19,590 --> 00:18:21,390
I just want to apologize.

296
00:18:21,550 --> 00:18:23,970
I'm really sorry I was a baby.

297
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:27,730
That's ridiculous. Rachel, we were all babies once.

298
00:18:30,310 --> 00:18:33,150
- Oh, you mean today.     - Yeah.

299
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:37,070
Yeah, and you know, you deserve to win.

300
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:38,860
And I was thinking about it.

301
00:18:39,030 --> 00:18:42,410
If you're Monica's maid of honor, I get to be yours.

302
00:18:42,570 --> 00:18:45,120
- Oh, yeah.     - Yeah.

303
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:50,120
When Monica and Chandler got engaged, I put some stuff together.

304
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:53,500
- Just in case.     - Oh, that's so sweet. Thanks.

305
00:18:53,670 --> 00:18:57,050
Here is a book of poetry that I know Monica loves.

306
00:18:57,210 --> 00:18:59,510
Oh, God, this is funny. Look.

307
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:03,180
Here's a picture from one Halloween when she dressed up as a bride.

308
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,180
She made me carry her train...

309
00:19:05,350 --> 00:19:08,600
...which was weird because I was Wonder Woman.

310
00:19:10,270 --> 00:19:13,020
Oh, and here's a little purse that I found.

311
00:19:13,190 --> 00:19:16,070
I just thought they could hold the rings in there.

312
00:19:16,230 --> 00:19:18,940
- Oh.     - Something. And...

313
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:23,660
...vintage handkerchiefs, you know, because people cry at weddings.

314
00:19:23,820 --> 00:19:26,490
I'm just gonna grab a couple of these.

315
00:19:27,450 --> 00:19:29,870
This stuff is great.

316
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:32,620
I forgot this was in here.

317
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:38,550
This was the garter that I was saving for my wedding.

318
00:19:38,710 --> 00:19:42,760
And I wanted it to be Monica's "something borrowed."

319
00:19:43,010 --> 00:19:44,430
And it's blue.

320
00:19:47,310 --> 00:19:48,810
Yeah.

321
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:53,900
Rach, I think that you should be Monica's maid of honor.

322
00:19:55,810 --> 00:19:57,820
You do?

323
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:01,860
- Why?     - Because I think it means more to you.

324
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:04,820
But, Pheebs, honey, you earned it.

325
00:20:04,990 --> 00:20:07,030
It's fine. I mean, this is something...

326
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:11,120
...that you've been thinking about since you were, what, 14?

327
00:20:11,290 --> 00:20:14,500
No, I was 10. I just developed early.

328
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,130
Man alive!

329
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:21,710
- Hey, what's going on?     - Hey!

330
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:25,130
We decided Rachel is going to be your maid of honor.

331
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:27,800
Oh, that's great!

332
00:20:27,970 --> 00:20:31,270
Oh, wow. Okay, we really have to start planning.

333
00:20:31,430 --> 00:20:33,640
I have really specific ideas.

334
00:20:33,890 --> 00:20:36,060
We should meet four times a week.

335
00:20:36,230 --> 00:20:39,650
Come to my place, we'll get together before work.

336
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:43,110
What do you say, 6:30, my place? So excited!

337
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:53,330
Yeah, okay. You laugh now.

338
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,040
She's gonna be yours.

339
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,060
Great nap.

340
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:15,270
It really was.

341
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:35,450
Dude, what the hell are you doing?

342
00:21:36,370 --> 00:21:38,250
God!

343
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:46,050
Excuse me.

